    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 4th with a clear emphasis on high-ceiling matchups against questionable opposing rotations. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) secures the top spot in our rankings today; his favorable matchup against J.T. Ginn is further bolstered by a 5% wind-out advantage and a premium spot in the two-hole, making him our highest-efficiency play. **Trea Turner** (79.40) and **Kyle Schwarber** (78.21) follow closely, both capitalizing on a juicy matchup against Lucas Giolito. While both face slight dynamic platoon regression, their elite base projections and the favorable park factor make them pillars of our offense today. **Christian Yelich** (75.84) also grades out as a strong play; even with a minor efficiency tax for facing an elite defensive catcher, his lead-off role against Adrian Houser provides the volume needed for a high-floor performance.\n\nThe lineup construction reflects a calculated risk regarding our fringe starters. **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) earned the nod over potential alternatives due to an 11% dynamic platoon bump and the prime lead-off slot, which overrides his lower raw base projection. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Kazuma Okamoto** (43.40); he remains in the lineup despite a difficult assignment against Chris Sale. His score is suppressed by Sale's elite skill set, but his 7% platoon advantage keeps him above our \"below floor\" threshold for today. Notably, **Gary Sanchez** (55.92) is our most precarious start, pending official lineup confirmation; his reliance on Houser's 4.75 xERA is the primary factor keeping him in the mix. Among our reserves, **Junior Caminero**, **Colt Keith**, and **Carson Benge** were excluded strictly due to the schedule, as our roster depth is currently limited by team off-days. We are continuing to monitor the status of **Hyeseong Kim**, who remains ineligible while rostered at Oklahoma City. \n\nAs we look toward the remainder of the week, managers should keep a close eye on the confirmed batting orders for **Gary Sanchez**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Christian Yelich**, **Yordan Alvarez**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. A shift out of their projected roles could significantly impact their efficiency scores, particularly for **Yordan Alvarez**, whose xwOBA of 0.454 makes him a must-start regardless of the marginal SP disadvantage he faces against Jared Jones. With **Zac Veen**, **Luke Raley**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Luis Pena**, **Pedro Ramirez**, and **Jose Fernandez** ready to fill gaps, the Zebras are well-positioned to maintain pressure in the SB and power categories throughout the week.",
